`secondArr.map(mapper)` allocates an array of every mapped value, then the `Set` constructor walks that array. Adding straight into the `Set` in a `for` loop keeps the same mapper calls and the same `delete`-on-match rule (`[2.1, 2.2]` against `[2.3, 3.4]` with `Math.floor` stays `[2.1]`).

